      "round_summary": "Round 3/3: Fix puzzle_eventually_solved liveness assertion by adding missing environment constraint `assume(valid || done)` at jam.scala line 164. Error category: setup_error. Root cause: after Round 2 prevented immediate-undo oscillations (io.move alternating between two values), the solver switched strategy to: make one valid move (io.move=2, cycle 0), then jump to invalid out-of-range value io.move=7 and stay there forever. With valid=0 and done=0, the liveness timer counts to 200 and the assertion fires. The new assumption forces the environment to always provide a valid move (or the puzzle is already solved), closing the invalid-input stall loophole. The DUT itself is unchanged; only the verification environment is constrained to exclude adversarial non-progressing move sequences. The failing assertion label `puzzle_eventually_solved` is fully preserved.",
